Requirements :
- User creates a logger specifies the destination types and the destination paths
- The user can call methods like logger.error(message) and logger.info(), logger.warning() these would be utilised by the users to log some stuff..
- There can be different destination types and different kinds of formatting and hence the logger should support that and be extensible..
- The user can actually write the destinations based on the different log level types..


Entities :
- Logger
- LogHandlerInterface
- LogProcessorInterface
- LogFormatterInterface
- FileLogProcessor
- ConsoleLogProcessor
- ErrorLogFormatter
- WarningLogFormatter
- ErrorLogHandler
- WarningLogHandler
- Logtypes ENUM
- DestinationTypes ENUM


Logger :  HashMap<LogType, LogHandler>, configureHandler(LogType, DestinationType, destination(optional)), error(), info(), debug()
LogProcessorInterface : processMessage(String message)
LogFormatterInterface : formatMessage(message) - > formatted message.
FileLogProcessor implements LogProcessorInterface : processMessage(message) - > process the message based on the fact that the destination type is a file might require some
additional formatting like putting the message in JSON/XML or remain as it is....
ErrorLogFormatter implements LogFormatterInterface : formatMessage(message) - > formats the message based on the Logtype and returns that message.
LogHandlerInterface : handleMessage(message) - > it just handles the incoming message based on the type of log and the destination type and configurations.
ErrorLogHandler : logProcessorInterface, logFormatterInterface, handleMessage(message)
LogTypes : ERROR, INFO, DEBUG
DestinationTypes : FILE, CONSOLE etc...





